.Sh CAVEATS
.ad l
Input that contains lowercase hex digits isn't handled gracefully,
often producing gibberish or an unhelpful error message.
This happens because lowercase letters are interpreted as commands in
.Xr dc 1 ,
and only uppercase
.Pq Li A\(enF
is used to specify values in radices greater than 10.
.if \n(.l<=(\n(.Hu*110u) .Pp
To work around this limitation,
add the following alias to your shell's startup profile:
.Bd -literal -offset 4n
.Sm off
.Cm alias \~ Nm No = Qq Ev LANG Ns = Ar C No \~ Nm tr \~ \
\(aq Bo a-f Bc \(aq\~ \
\(aq Bo A-F Bc \(aq\~ \
| \~ Nm
.Sm on
.Ed
